# Vengeful Villagers: with its only target gone the ability does nothing (CR 608.2b), so there is no sacrifice to offer and no
# counter to place. Bot1 attacks and the trigger targets Bot2's Ornithopter; in response Bot2 Bolts it, and Bot1 keeps all its Mox
# Pearls (a sacrifice prompt would otherwise be pending and the final pass would not reach Main2).

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Pearl
Mox Pearl
Mox Pearl
Mox Pearl
Mox Pearl
Vengeful Villagers
Island
Island x13

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Ruby
Lightning Bolt
Ornithopter
Plains x17

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl#1.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl#2.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl#3.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl#4.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Vengeful Villagers.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T3 Bot1.DeclareAttackers]
Bot1.Attack(Vengeful Villagers > Bot2)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Graveyard.Count = 0
Bot2.Graveyard = Ornithopter; Lightning Bolt
